  "content": {
    "id": "p38-q14-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "Let $P(x,6)$ lie on $y=f(x)$. Find the new $y$-coordinate of $P$ on each of the following.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p38-q14-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$y=\\frac{1}{3}f(x)+1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3$",
          "worked": "Dilate vertically by a factor of $\\frac{1}{3}$, then translate up $1$ unit. Since $f(x)=6$,\n$$\\begin{align*}y_{\\mathrm{new}}&=\\frac{1}{3}(6)+1\\\\y_{\\mathrm{new}}&=3.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q14-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$y=2-\\frac{1}{2}f(x)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-1$",
          "worked": "Dilate vertically by a factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$ and reflect in the $x$-axis, then translate up $2$ units. Since $f(x)=6$,\n$$\\begin{align*}y_{\\mathrm{new}}&=2-\\frac{1}{2}(6)\\\\y_{\\mathrm{new}}&=-1.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q14-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$y=\\frac{f(x)-1}{3}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{5}{3}$",
          "worked": "Translate down $1$ unit, then dilate vertically by a factor of $\\frac{1}{3}$. Since $f(x)=6$,\n$$\\begin{align*}y_{\\mathrm{new}}&=\\frac{6-1}{3}\\\\y_{\\mathrm{new}}&=\\frac{5}{3}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q14-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$y=\\frac{2f(x)+1}{4}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{13}{4}$",
          "worked": "Dilate vertically by a factor of $2$, translate up $1$ unit, then dilate vertically by a factor of $\\frac{1}{4}$. Since $f(x)=6$,\n$$\\begin{align*}y_{\\mathrm{new}}&=\\frac{2(6)+1}{4}\\\\y_{\\mathrm{new}}&=\\frac{13}{4}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 58
      }
    ]
  },
